# v0.23 (round 356), decision 33: a line break is the only statement
# separator Whence has, and it is REQUIRED between two statements. "1 2" was
# two valid top-level statements in both the host and the guest until this
# version; now both refuse it. The wording differs by design (the host
# raises an exception with a column, the guest returns a miss with a line —
# `tests/test_v22.py::test_parse_error_wording_is_not_a_guest_contract`),
# so what is checked here is the refusal and the line, not the sentence.
check "two statements with no separator are refused": missed(parse_whence("1 2"))
check "...and the same two statements parse on two lines":
  not missed(parse_whence("1\n2")) and len((parse_whence("1\n2")).stmts) == 2
